    <script type="application/ld+json">{"mainEntity":{"headline":"Spirulina platensis protects against microcystin-LR-induced toxicity in rats","description":"Microcystis aeruginosa produces an abundant cyanotoxin (microcystins (MCs) in freshwater supplies. MCs have adverse health hazards to animals and humans. Microcystin-leucine-arginine (microcystin-LR or MC-LR) is the most studied among these MCs due to their high toxicity. So, this study was designed to evaluate the possible therapeutic role of the natural algal food supplement, Spirulina platensis (SP), against MC-LR-induced toxic effects in male Wistar rats. Forty rats were randomly divided into five groups. Control and SP groups orally administered distilled water and SP (1000 mg/kg/daily), respectively, for 21 days. MC-LR group was intraperitoneally injected with MC-LR (10 μg/kg/day) for 14 days. MC-LR-SP500 and MC-LR-SP1000 groups were orally treated with SP (500 and 1000 mg/kg, respectively) for 7 days and concomitantly with MC-LR for 14 days. MC-LR induced oxidative hepatorenal damage, cardiotoxicity, and neurotoxicity greatly, which was represented by reduction of reduced glutathione content and the activities of glutathione peroxidase, catalase, and superoxide dismutase and elevation of concentrations of nitric oxide and malondialdehyde in renal, hepatic, brain, and heart tissues. In addition, it increased serum levels of urea, creatinine, tumor necrosis factor-alfa, interleukin-1beta and interleukin-6 and serum activities of alkaline phosphatase, aspartate aminotransferase, alanine aminotransferase, lactate dehydrogenase, creatine kinase, and creatine kinase-MB. However, S. platensis restored normal levels of measured serum parameters, ameliorated MC-LR-induced oxidative damage, and normalized tissue antioxidant biomarkers. In conclusion, SP alleviated MC-induced organ toxicities by mitigating oxidative and nitrosative stress and lipid peroxidation.","datePublished":"2021-09-17T00:00:00Z","dateModified":"2021-09-17T00:00:00Z","pageStart":"11320","pageEnd":"11331","sameAs":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11356-021-16481-y","keywords":["\n                Microalgae\n              ","MC-LR","Antioxidant","Oxidative stress","Reactive oxygen species","Liver","Kidney","Heart","Brain","Environment","general","Environmental Chemistry","Ecotoxicology","Environmental Health","Atmospheric Protection/Air Quality Control/Air Pollution","Waste Water Technology / Water Pollution Control / Water Management / Aquatic Pollution"],"image":["https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11356-021-16481-y/MediaObjects/11356_2021_16481_Fig1_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11356-021-16481-y/MediaObjects/11356_2021_16481_Fig2_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11356-021-16481-y/MediaObjects/11356_2021_16481_Fig3_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11356-021-16481-y/MediaObjects/11356_2021_16481_Fig4_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11356-021-16481-y/MediaObjects/11356_2021_16481_Fig5_HTML.png"],"isPartOf":{"name":"Environmental Science and Pollution Research","issn":["1614-7499","0944-1344"],"volumeNumber":"29","@type":["Periodical","PublicationVolume"]},"publisher":{"name":"Springer Berlin Heidelberg","logo":{"url":"https://www.springernature.com/app-sn/public/images/logo-springernature.png","@type":"ImageObject"},"@type":"Organization"},"author":[{"name":"\n                              Mousa O. Germoush","affiliation":[{"name":"Jouf University","address":{"name":"Biology Department, College of Science, Jouf University, Sakaka, Saudi Arabia","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Maged M. A. Fouda","affiliation":[{"name":"Jouf University","address":{"name":"Biology Department, College of Science, Jouf University, Sakaka, Saudi Arabia","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Al-Azhar University, Assuit Branch","address":{"name":"Department of Zoology, Faculty of Science, Al-Azhar University, Assuit Branch, Assuit, Egypt","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Mohamed Kamel","affiliation":[{"name":"Cairo University","address":{"name":"Department of Medicine and Infectious Diseases, Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, Cairo University, Giza, Egypt","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Mohamed M. Abdel-Daim","url":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-4341-2713","affiliation":[{"name":"Batterjee Medical College","address":{"name":"Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Pharmacy Program, Batterjee Medical College, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Suez Canal University","address":{"name":"Pharmacology Department, Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, Suez Canal University, Ismailia, Egypt","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"email":"abdeldaim.m@vet.suez.edu.eg","@type":"Person"}],"isAccessibleForFree":false,"hasPart":{"isAccessibleForFree":false,"cssSelector":".main-content","@type":"WebPageElement"},"@type":"ScholarlyArticle"},"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage"}</script>

        
        
